#
# File:         sdkconfig.defaults.mf35
# Module:       Build / ESP-IDF defaults, Makerfabs ESP32-S3 Parallel TFT 3.5" layer
#
# Purpose:      What the Makerfabs ESP32-S3 Parallel TFT with Touch 3.5" build
#               changes from sdkconfig.defaults and sdkconfig.defaults.esp32s3.
#               platformio.ini names this file for the board's environments
#               through SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS (board_build.cmake_extra_args).
#               IDF 5.3.1 still reads "<file>.<target>" after each file it is
#               given (tools/cmake/kconfig.cmake), so the order is
#               sdkconfig.defaults, sdkconfig.defaults.esp32s3, then this
#               file, and a later value wins: this layer only undoes what the
#               S3 layer wrote for the Waveshare stick.
#
#               The part (hardware v1.0): ESP32-S3-WROOM-1-N16R2 (read on the bench: "Embedded
#               PSRAM 2MB (AP_3v3)", 16 MB quad flash), with a CP2104 bridge
#               to UART0 as well as the chip's own USB. Sources are in
#               src/board.h, BBS_BOARD_MF_S3PAR35.
#
#               PlatformIO keeps the generated sdkconfig.<env>, a value it
#               already holds wins over this file, and it does not watch this
#               file: delete sdkconfig.makerfabs_s3_par35* after editing here,
#               and check the generated file. A value outside its Kconfig
#               range is discarded, not clamped.
#
# Targets:      ESP32-S3 (ESP-IDF 5.3.1)
# See also:     sdkconfig.defaults, sdkconfig.defaults.esp32s3, platformio.ini
#
